If $vb(X)$ is a Gaussian vector, $matbold(A)$ an $m times n$ matrix and $vb(b) in RR^m$, then $matbold(A) vb(X) + vb(b)$ is also a Gaussian vector.

For any $vb(u) in RR^n$, let $vb(v) = matbold(A)^TT vb(u)$; then
$
  vb(u)^TT (matbold(A) vb(X) + vb(b)) & = vb(v)^TT vb(X) + sum_(i=1)^n u_i b_i,
$
a Gaussian random variable plus a constant, hence a Gaussian random variable.
